INT. NEW DAWN FERTILITY CENTER - LOBBY - MORNING

SERIES OF SHOTS:

-- A fish tank, bubbling. Three clownfish circle a plastic castle.

-- A clock on the wall: 8:02.

-- Hands on a clipboard. Rings. Nervous pens.

Karina Bell, 30s, stands at the reception desk in scrubs, and beside her, Kari Beal, 20s, a trainee, also in scrubs. They share a look. The name tags are a coin flip.

KARINA
No, I'm Karina. You're Kari.

KARI
That's what I said.

KARINA
You said Karina.

KARI
It's eight in the morning.

Dev Anand, 30s, and his wife Mira, 30s, enter holding hands too tightly.

ON PHONE (INSERT): Dev's screen. A text from his mother: "DID YOU GO YET? WE ARE PRAYING."

DEV
(pocketing it)
She's praying.

MIRA
She's always praying.

DEV
Her prayers are very specific.

Mira laughs. Almost.

MONTAGE - THE WAITING ROOM

-- 8:20. Dev reads a magazine upside down.

-- 8:44. Mira scrolls her phone. ON PHONE: "How to not panic during IVF consult."

-- 9:15. The clownfish. Still circling.

-- 9:40. Karina and Kari argue over a chart. Karina holds it higher. Kari jumps for it.

KARINA
Kari, give me the file.

KARI
Karina, I'm helping.

DEV
(to Mira, whispering)
Which one's our nurse?

MIRA
Both. Neither. I can't tell.

Dr. Odette Fontaine, 50s, steps out of a back room. Silver bob, calm, a stethoscope like jewelry.

DR. FONTAINE
Mr. and Mrs. Anand? Come in, please.

They stand. Dev is shaking.

DEV
Mira, honey, I love you, and I'm scared.

MIRA
Dev, I love you, and I'm also scared. Walk.

They follow Dr. Fontaine. The door closes.

INT. NEW DAWN FERTILITY CENTER - HALLWAY - LATER

SUPER: "THREE WEEKS LATER."

Dev and Mira stand outside the exam room. In Mira's hand, a small white stick. She turns it over.

ON PHONE: Mira's text to her sister: "ITS POSITIVE!!!! DONT TELL MA"

Dev reads it over her shoulder.

DEV
You texted your sister before me?

MIRA
You were in the bathroom.

DEV
I'm always in the bathroom!

Mira bursts out laughing, tears coming now. He pulls her in.

Suddenly the door at the end of the hall bangs open.

A man in a pharmacy delivery jacket, NERVOUS COURIER, 20s, rushes in with a cooler.

COURIER
Is there a, uh, Odette? I need a signature. This thing's been in my car for six hours.

KARINA (O.S.)
Don't sign! It's the wrong clinic!

KARI (O.S.)
He's wearing the wrong jacket!

The courier looks at Dev and Mira. Mira looks at Dev.

DEV
Is that, is that our...

COURIER
(checking tag)
Anand? Yeah?

MIRA
(a gasp)
That's the second batch!

DEV
(grabbing the cooler)
We've got a baby on the way and a cooler in the hall! Everybody stay calm!

Karina and Kari run in from opposite ends of the hall and collide. Charts everywhere.

KARINA
Kari!

KARI
Karina!

They both reach for the cooler. Dev holds it above his head. Dr. Fontaine steps out of the exam room, sees the chaos, folds her arms.

DR. FONTAINE
Is this a delivery, or a rugby match?

Everyone freezes. A beat.

MIRA
(softly)
Both.

SERIES OF SHOTS:

-- The cooler, opened. Inside: a small vase of flowers and a card.

-- ON CARD: "From Ma. We are praying. P.S. Congratulations."

-- Dev and Mira stare. Then look at each other. Then at the ceiling.

-- Karina and Kari, side by side, wiping their eyes.

DEV
(soft)
How did she know?

MIRA
(wiping her eyes)
My sister told her.

DEV
Of course she did.

Mira leans her head on his shoulder. The clownfish circle on.

FADE OUT.
